<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>Cameron Cavicchiolo — Projects</title>
<meta name="description" content="Tools Cameron Cavicchiolo, a Michigan State supply chain student, has built with AI.">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wdth,wght@62..125,400..800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --paper: #EEF1F4;
    --ink: #17212B;
    --muted: #55626F;
    --rule: #C5CDD5;
    --blue: #1F4E79;
    --signal: #F2C230;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px);
    padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px);
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --paper: #121A22;
      --ink: #E6EBF0;
      --muted: #97A4B1;
      --rule: #2C3946;
      --blue: #7FB2E0;
      --signal: #F2C230;
    }
  }
  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: inherit; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Archivo", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
    font-variation-settings: "wdth" 100;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .wrap {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem 3rem;
  }

  /* Hero: the name is the one bold move */
  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-variation-settings: "wdth" 125;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 9vw, 5.75rem);
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .stripe {
    width: 4.5rem;
    height: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--signal);
    margin: 1.75rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .intro {
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .intro + .intro {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .contact {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--blue);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--signal); }
  a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--signal);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Projects as rows, not cards */
  h2 {
    margin: 4.5rem 0 0;
    font-variation-settings: "wdth" 110;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }
  .projects {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 3px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .project {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 10rem;
    gap: 0.5rem 2rem;
    padding: 1.75rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .project h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-variation-settings: "wdth" 115;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .project p { margin: 0; max-width: 34rem; }
  .built {
    margin-top: 0.6rem !important;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    align-self: start;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .soon { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }

  footer {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .wrap { padding-top: 3rem; }
    .project { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .links { flex-direction: row; gap: 1.25rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="wrap">

  <header>
    <h1>Cameron<br>Cavicchiolo</h1>
    <div class="stripe" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <p class="intro">Supply chain management senior at Michigan State, graduating summer 2027. I build working tools with AI to solve problems I actually have.</p>
    <p class="intro">I don't have a coding background. Everything here was built with Claude, and each project taught me how to break a messy problem into steps a computer can follow. I've interned in supply chain at Adient and Kuehne+Nagel.</p>
    <div class="contact">
      <!-- Replace with your real LinkedIn URL and email -->
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/YOUR-LINKEDIN">LinkedIn</a>
      <a href="mailto:YOUR-EMAIL@example.com">Email</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/cams-creations">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
    <h2 id="projects-heading">Projects</h2>
    <ul class="projects">

      <li class="project">
        <div>
          <h3>Chess Coach</h3>
          <p>Pulls my rapid games from Chess.com, runs them through the Stockfish chess engine to find where I lose the most, and writes me a weekly coaching summary.</p>
          <p class="built">Built with Claude, the Chess.com API, and Stockfish</p>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://cams-creations.github.io/chess-coach/">Live site</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/cams-creations/chess-coach">Code</a>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="project">
        <div>
          <h3>Booking Site for a Mobile Detailer</h3>
          <p>A booking website for a Metro Detroit car detailer. Customers pick a detail package, then choose a date and time. Shown here as a demo with the business's contact details removed.</p>
          <p class="built">Built with Claude as part of my freelance work making sites for local service businesses</p>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://cams-creations.github.io/booking-demo/">Live demo</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/cams-creations/booking-demo">Code</a>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="project">
        <div>
          <h3>Calendar</h3>
          <!-- Replace this sentence with what the calendar does -->
          <p>[One or two sentences on what the calendar does and why you built it.]</p>
          <p class="built">Built with Claude</p>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <span class="soon">Coming soon</span>
        </div>
      </li>

    </ul>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p>Questions about any of these? I'm happy to walk through how they work.</p>
  </footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
